# UI/UX Design Standards —

## 🎯 Core Principles

### Design Philosophy

- **Professional & Modern**: Clean, minimalist interfaces that prioritize clarity and efficiency
- **Unified Experience**: Consistent design language across all interfaces (debug, monitoring, dashboards)
- **User-Centered**: Design decisions based on user needs, not aesthetics alone
- **Accessibility First**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance minimum, AAA where possible
- **Performance**: Fast, responsive interfaces that don't compromise functionality

### Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics

1. **Visibility of system status**: Always show what's happening
2. **Match real world**: Use familiar concepts and language
3. **User control**: Allow undo/redo, easy navigation
4. **Consistency**: Same patterns across interfaces
5. **Error prevention**: Prevent errors before they occur
6. **Recognition over recall**: Visual cues, not memory
7. **Flexibility**: Shortcuts for power users
8. **Aesthetic minimalism**: Remove unnecessary elements
9. **Error recovery**: Clear, helpful error messages
10. **Help & documentation**: Easy to find when needed

## 🎨 Design Token System

### MANDATORY: Use Design Tokens, Never Hard-Code Values

All visual design must use CSS custom properties (design tokens) defined in a shared token system.

#### Color Tokens Structure

```css
:root {
  /* Brand Colors -  Identity */
  --color-brand-primary: #0066cc;        /* Primary blue - trust, technology */
  --color-brand-secondary: #ff6600;      /* Secondary orange - energy, action */
  --color-brand-accent: #00cc99;         /* Accent teal - innovation */

  /* Semantic Colors - Status & Feedback */
  --color-success: #22c55e;              /* Green - success, healthy */
  --color-success-light: #d1fae5;
  --color-success-dark: #065f46;

  --color-warning: #eab308;              /* Yellow - caution, attention */
  --color-warning-light: #fef3c7;
  --color-warning-dark: #92400e;

  --color-error: #ef4444;                 /* Red - error, critical */
  --color-error-light: #fee2e2;
  --color-error-dark: #991b1b;

  --color-info: #3b82f6;                  /* Blue - information */
  --color-info-light: #dbeafe;
  --color-info-dark: #1e40af;

  /* Neutral Colors - Backgrounds & Text */
  --color-neutral-50: #f9fafb;
  --color-neutral-100: #f3f4f6;
  --color-neutral-200: #e5e7eb;
  --color-neutral-300: #d1d5db;
  --color-neutral-400: #9ca3af;
  --color-neutral-500: #6b7280;
  --color-neutral-600: #4b5563;
  --color-neutral-700: #374151;
  --color-neutral-800: #1f2937;
  --color-neutral-900: #111827;

  /* Surface Colors */
  --color-bg-primary: var(--color-neutral-50);
  --color-bg-secondary: var(--color-neutral-100);
  --color-surface: #ffffff;
  --color-surface-elevated: #ffffff;

  /* Text Colors */
  --color-text-primary: var(--color-neutral-900);
  --color-text-secondary: var(--color-neutral-600);
  --color-text-tertiary: var(--color-neutral-400);
  --color-text-inverse: #ffffff;

  /* Border Colors */
  --color-border-default: var(--color-neutral-200);
  --color-border-focus: var(--color-brand-primary);
  --color-border-error: var(--color-error);

  /* Shadow Tokens */
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  --shadow-md: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  --shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  --shadow-xl: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);

  /* Spacing Scale (8px base unit) */
  --space-1: 0.25rem;  /* 4px */
  --space-2: 0.5rem;   /* 8px */
  --space-3: 0.75rem;  /* 12px */
  --space-4: 1rem;     /* 16px */
  --space-5: 1.25rem;  /* 20px */
  --space-6: 1.5rem;   /* 24px */
  --space-8: 2rem;     /* 32px */
  --space-10: 2.5rem;  /* 40px */
  --space-12: 3rem;    /* 48px */
  --space-16: 4rem;    /* 64px */
  --space-20: 5rem;    /* 80px */

  /* Typography Scale */
  --font-family-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto,
                      'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-family-mono: 'SF Mono', Monaco, 'Cascadia Code', 'Courier New', monospace;

  --font-size-xs: 0.75rem;    /* 12px */
  --font-size-sm: 0.875rem;    /* 14px */
  --font-size-base: 1rem;     /* 16px */
  --font-size-lg: 1.125rem;    /* 18px */
  --font-size-xl: 1.25rem;     /* 20px */
  --font-size-2xl: 1.5rem;     /* 24px */
  --font-size-3xl: 2rem;       /* 32px */
  --font-size-4xl: 2.5rem;     /* 40px */

  --font-weight-normal: 400;
  --font-weight-medium: 500;
  --font-weight-semibold: 600;
  --font-weight-bold: 700;

  --line-height-tight: 1.25;
  --line-height-normal: 1.5;
  --line-height-relaxed: 1.75;

  /* Border Radius */
  --radius-sm: 0.25rem;   /* 4px */
  --radius-md: 0.5rem;    /* 8px */
  --radius-lg: 0.75rem;   /* 12px */
  --radius-xl: 1rem;      /* 16px */
  --radius-full: 9999px;

  /* Transitions */
  --transition-fast: 150ms ease-in-out;
  --transition-base: 200ms ease-in-out;
  --transition-slow: 300ms ease-in-out;

  /* Z-Index Scale */
  --z-base: 0;
  --z-dropdown: 1000;
  --z-sticky: 1020;
  --z-fixed: 1030;
  --z-modal-backdrop: 1040;
  --z-modal: 1050;
  --z-popover: 1060;
  --z-tooltip: 1070;
}
```

## 📐 Layout & Spacing

### Grid System

- Use CSS Grid or Flexbox for layouts
- Standard container max-width: `1200px` (large screens)
- Consistent gutters: `var(--space-4)` (16px) minimum
- Responsive breakpoints:
  - Mobile: `< 640px`
  - Tablet: `640px - 1024px`
  - Desktop: `> 1024px`

### Spacing Principles

- **Consistent Rhythm**: Use spacing scale (8px base unit)
- **Vertical Spacing**: `var(--space-4)` minimum between sections
- **Card Padding**: `var(--space-6)` (24px) standard
- **Component Gap**: `var(--space-3)` to `var(--space-4)` for related elements

## 🎨 Component Patterns

### Cards & Containers

```css
.card {
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-6);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  transition: box-shadow var(--transition-base);
}

.card:hover {
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.card-header {
  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
}
```

### Status Indicators

- **OK/Success**: Green (`--color-success`)
- **Warning**: Yellow (`--color-warning`)
- **Error/Critical**: Red (`--color-error`)
- **Info**: Blue (`--color-info`)
- **Neutral/Unknown**: Gray (`--color-neutral-500`)

Always combine color with:
- Icon/Symbol (checkmark, warning, error, info)
- Text label (semantic, not just color)
- Shape/Background for contrast

### Badges & Tags

```css
.badge {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

.badge-success {
  background: var(--color-success-light);
  color: var(--color-success-dark);
}

.badge-warning {
  background: var(--color-warning-light);
  color: var(--color-warning-dark);
}

.badge-error {
  background: var(--color-error-light);
  color: var(--color-error-dark);
}
```

### Buttons

- Primary: Brand color, high contrast
- Secondary: Outline style
- Danger: Error color
- Disabled: Gray with reduced opacity
- Minimum touch target: `44px × 44px`
- Clear hover/focus/active states

### Forms & Inputs

- Clear labels above or beside inputs
- Error states: Red border + error message
- Success states: Green border (when applicable)
- Focus states: Brand color outline
- Placeholder text: `var(--color-text-tertiary)`
- Helper text: `var(--font-size-sm)`, `var(--color-text-secondary)`

## 🔄 Interaction States

Every interactive element MUST have:

1. **Default**: Standard appearance
2. **Hover**: Subtle elevation or color change
3. **Focus**: Visible outline (keyboard navigation)
4. **Active**: Pressed/pressed state
5. **Disabled**: Reduced opacity, no interaction

```css
.button {
  transition: all var(--transition-base);
}

.button:hover {
  transform: translateY(-1px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.button:focus {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-border-focus);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.button:active {
  transform: translateY(0);
}

.button:disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
  pointer-events: none;
}
```

## 📱 Responsive Design

### Mobile-First Approach

1. Design for mobile first (`< 640px`)
2. Enhance for tablet (`640px+`)
3. Optimize for desktop (`1024px+`)

### Responsive Patterns

- Stack columns on mobile
- Hide non-essential information
- Touch-friendly targets (`44px` minimum)
- Simplified navigation (hamburger menu)
- Optimized images and assets

## ♿ Accessibility Requirements

### WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance

- **Color Contrast**:
  - Normal text: 4.5:1 minimum
  - Large text (18px+): 3:1 minimum
  - UI components: 3:1 minimum
- **Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive elements accessible via keyboard
- **Focus Indicators**: Visible focus states for all focusable elements
- **Alt Text**: Descriptive alt text for all images
- **ARIA Labels**: Use ARIA labels when semantic HTML insufficient
- **Screen Reader Support**: Proper heading hierarchy, landmarks

### Color Accessibility

- **Never rely on color alone**: Combine with icons, shapes, or text
- **Provide alternatives**: Don't use only red/green (colorblind users)
- **Test contrast**: Use tools to verify contrast ratios

## 📊 Dashboard Design Patterns

### Layout Strategies

1. **Screenfit**: All content visible without scrolling (ideal for at-a-glance)
2. **Overflow**: Scrollable content when needed
3. **Detail-on-Demand**: Show details in tooltips/modals
4. **Multi-Page**: Distribute content across tabs/pages

### Information Hierarchy

1. **Primary**: Most important metrics (top, larger, bold)
2. **Secondary**: Supporting information (middle)
3. **Tertiary**: Details, history (bottom, smaller)

### Visual Representation Patterns

- **Numbers**: Large, prominent for key metrics
- **Charts**: Use appropriate chart types (line for trends, bar for comparisons)
- **Sparklines**: Small trend indicators without axes
- **Icons**: Semantic icons for quick recognition
- **Tables**: For detailed data comparison

### Card Types (Dashboard)

- **Status Card**: Current state + status indicator
- **Trend Card**: Current value + trend chart
- **Utilization Card**: Current value + progress visualization
- **Details Card**: Attribute-value pairs
- **Events Card**: List of events/alerts

## 🎯 Design Quality Checklist

### Before Implementation

- [ ] All colors use design tokens (no hard-coded hex values)
- [ ] Spacing uses spacing scale
- [ ] Typography uses typography scale
- [ ] Interactive elements have all states (hover, focus, active, disabled)
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA standards
- [ ] Responsive design tested on mobile/tablet/desktop
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works for all interactions
- [ ] Focus indicators visible and clear
- [ ] Error states have clear messaging
- [ ] Loading states provide feedback

### Code Quality

- [ ] CSS uses CSS custom properties (tokens)
- [ ] No inline styles
- [ ] Consistent naming conventions (BEM or similar)
- [ ] Semantic HTML structure
- [ ] ARIA labels where needed
- [ ] No accessibility violations

## 🚫 Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid

1. **Hard-coded colors**: Always use tokens
2. **Inconsistent spacing**: Stick to spacing scale
3. **Missing focus states**: Critical for accessibility
4. **Color-only indicators**: Add icons/text
5. **Tiny touch targets**: Minimum 44px
6. **Poor contrast**: Test all color combinations
7. **Inconsistent patterns**: Reuse components
8. **Unclear error messages**: Be specific and helpful
9. **No loading states**: Always show progress
10. **Ignoring mobile**: Mobile-first approach

